Project Ownership & Usage Policy
Copyright & Ownership

All source code, documentation, designs, assets, and other materials contained within this repository are the original work and intellectual property of the repository owner, unless explicitly stated otherwise.

All rights are reserved. By accessing, downloading, modifying, or contributing to this project, you acknowledge that the original ownership and copyright remain with the repository owner.

Forking & Redistribution

Forking this repository is permitted, provided that the following conditions are respected:

Explicit Credit: You must clearly and visibly credit the original author and link back to this repository in your fork, documentation, and any public distribution.
No Misrepresentation: You may not claim the original code, project, or its development as your own.
Preserve Notices: All existing copyright, ownership, and attribution notices must remain intact.
Upstream Contributions: Any improvements, features, bug fixes, or general enhancements developed in a fork must be submitted back to the original repository through a pull request, provided they do not contain malicious code, harmful functionality, or otherwise compromise the integrity or security of the project.
No Malicious Modifications: Forks may not introduce malware, spyware, backdoors, credential theft, destructive functionality, or other intentionally harmful code while retaining association with this project.
Commercial Use & Monetization

Commercial use is strictly prohibited without prior explicit written permission from the original author.

This includes, but is not limited to:

Selling the software or modified versions of it.
Incorporating the code into commercial products or services.
Offering the project as part of a paid subscription, service, or platform.
Using the project to generate revenue directly or indirectly.
Redistributing the project as part of a commercial package.
Monetizing forks, derivatives, or adaptations of this project.

Commercial licensing may be granted on a case-by-case basis.

Any commercial arrangement must be explicitly discussed and agreed upon in writing beforehand. Compensation, royalties, licensing fees, revenue sharing, and other terms may be negotiated individually.

Simply providing attribution does not grant commercial usage rights.

Contributions

Contributions are welcome, provided they align with the project's goals and standards.

By submitting a contribution, you acknowledge that:

Your contributions must be your original work or appropriately licensed.
Contributions must not contain malicious, harmful, or unauthorized functionality.
Contributions may be incorporated into the original project.
You retain ownership of your original contributions, unless otherwise agreed in writing.
You grant the project owner permission to use, modify, distribute, and maintain submitted contributions as part of this project.
Restrictions

You may not:

Claim ownership of this project or its original source code.
Remove or alter copyright and attribution notices.
Use this project commercially without written authorization.
Distribute modified versions without proper attribution.
Use this project as a foundation for malicious, deceptive, or harmful software.
Imply that your fork or derivative project is officially maintained or endorsed by the original author without permission.
